WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.530
Hello and welcome.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.750
Very good to be with you
and have your company.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.010
Now, my first guest in
this brand new series

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.220
is the Chinese dissident artist

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.520
and now author, Ai Weiwei.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.840
Starting off as a filmmaker
in the late seventies,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.460
he's now famed for his
provocative and political work.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.100
Perhaps best known for
his art installations,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.598
from the 14,000 life
jackets used by refugees

00:00:43.598 --> 00:00:46.320
he attached to a Berlin concert hall,

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.010
to filling a gallery in London

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:50.920
with 100 million
handcrafted sunflower seeds

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.990
to question the "made
in China" phenomenon.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:57.010
He has also disowned one
of his most famous designs,

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.943
the Bird's Nest Stadium
that was at the heart

00:00:58.943 --> 00:01:01.990
of the 2008 Beijing Olympics,

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.023
citing serious concerns

00:01:03.023 --> 00:01:06.660
over the Chinese government's
human rights record.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.180
Following the destruction of his studio

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.460
and imprisonment in China,

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.990
he left his home country
but continues to document,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.740
create and agitate.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:19.070
He joins me now from his
latest abode in Portugal,

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.520
sadly COVID travel restrictions means

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.570
we cannot be together in person.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.433
But, Ai Weiwei, welcome.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:27.748
Thank you.

00:01:27.748 --> 00:01:30.947
Your latest creation is
your book, your memoir,

00:01:30.947 --> 00:01:34.430
"A Thousand Years of Joys and Sorrows."

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.080
What have you learned about
yourself from writing it?

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.240
Well, I think the purpose
to writing this book

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.730
is to find out my
relations with my father.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.452
And I realized, during the detention,

00:01:49.452 --> 00:01:54.452
I realized most of our memories

00:01:54.473 --> 00:01:59.320
either being erased or
destroyed by the authority.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:04.320
So I think the most dangerous
this authority is doing

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:09.410
to authoritarian state is
trying to change the facts,

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.120
what happened in the past.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.390
So I have to establish
a real understanding

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.390
of my father's condition
in almost past 100 years,

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.120
and to write down what I know
and to leave this to my son.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.768
Yes, that's the big driving force,

00:02:29.768 --> 00:02:32.798
your son, who you say will
be your ultimate arbiter.

00:02:32.798 --> 00:02:35.741
I talked about you being imprisoned,

00:02:35.741 --> 00:02:40.530
being under arrest for charges
of a tax bill of millions.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.028
This was after your artistic activities

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:46.150
and speaking out against the
Chinese government online.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.640
But when you talk about your father,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.780
he was internally exiled.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.207
You were with him, you were
separate from your mother.

00:02:52.207 --> 00:02:54.450
He was exiled for being a poet

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.060
and a so-called, "intellectual."

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.790
And you lived in a hole
in the ground together.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.633
And I wonder, for you,

00:03:01.633 --> 00:03:05.663
how much that prepared you
for your own imprisonment?

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.809
Well, my father was exiled
in Xinjiang province

00:03:10.809 --> 00:03:15.809
where the Uyghur people today
have the re-education camps.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.630
So we are probably the
first group moved to there

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.650
to be re-educated.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.457
And my father spent about
20 years in that region

00:03:25.457 --> 00:03:29.233
and forbidden to write anything.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.680
So he's been doing hard labor

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.520
and also we're being punished
to live underground in a hole.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.703
So all those experience,

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.440
I later, much later realized
that made me become me today.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:56.170
And I would look at society
or a political system

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:02.590
with a different angle and a
very different perspective.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:05.560
And in terms of your situation now,

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.710
you're talking to me from Portugal,

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.825
are you able to go back to China?

00:04:09.825 --> 00:04:14.825
I don't think I can be
safely stay in China.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.589
Maybe they would allow
me to get into China

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:23.120
because I'm a Chinese citizen,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.068
but I wouldn't know I
would be safe in there.

00:04:27.068 --> 00:04:32.068
And also I will not know
if they would let me out.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.420
I talk to my mom almost daily,

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.510
and the last sentence she always
tell me, do not come back.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.260
She knows I may want to go back.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.897
So your mother's still there,

00:04:43.897 --> 00:04:45.518
but you can't get back.
Yes.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.817
What do you think would happen to you?

00:04:50.406 --> 00:04:51.600
Who knows.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.881
It's never, you never can predict.

00:04:53.881 --> 00:04:57.490
I know so many people disappeared.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:01.030
I know many people being
sentenced heavily for,

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.480
didn't do anything wrong.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.313
You just don't know.

00:05:04.313 --> 00:05:05.870
I mean, I suppose that's the thing.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.270
I went to the exhibition

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.046
that you held at the
Royal Academy in London,

00:05:10.046 --> 00:05:12.753
in which you recreated
some of those scenes

00:05:12.753 --> 00:05:15.302
of your own imprisonment, the 81 days.

00:05:15.302 --> 00:05:17.513
People may remember you
also kind of crowdfunded

00:05:17.513 --> 00:05:21.780
to pay the millions that
you were said to owe in tax.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:22.800
Some people were just throwing

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.859
the money in to your garden, I understand,

00:05:25.859 --> 00:05:27.810
with paper airplanes.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.630
But actually, I understand
you formed a bond

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.740
with the guards.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.070
They had to follow you everywhere,

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.080
to go to the toilet, to the shower,

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.360
that came across in the art
that you created about it.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.890
And those guards started
to ask you for advice,

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:42.723
is that right?

00:05:42.723 --> 00:05:44.989
About their own lives, their love lives.

00:05:44.989 --> 00:05:45.860
Yes.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.770
They also, they're soldiers,

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.100
but they're only very young, 20 years old,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.840
and they know nothing about outside world.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:00.176
The only thing they do is trying
to protect someone like me.

00:06:00.176 --> 00:06:02.330
They don't even know the name.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:05.980
So they will have a lot of
curiosity about the outside,

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.790
about everything in life.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:12.990
I think they are also just
like me, as prisoners.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:17.020
As youngsters, they
really like to know more

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:21.503
about sex or any experience like that.

00:06:21.503 --> 00:06:25.377
You know, I don't have a rich experience,

00:06:25.377 --> 00:06:26.886
but I still can tell them more.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:29.330
Good we've got the out at this point.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.380
But I was gonna say, of course,

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.420
some of your formative years in that time,

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:36.640
you went to New York and had
your own education, I'm sure.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.850
But I was gonna come to that.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.050
The guards that were tasked

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.240
with making sure you were
where you were meant to be,

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.715
you say they didn't know who you were.

00:06:45.715 --> 00:06:49.223
Do people in China know
who is Ai Weiwei is?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:55.220
Before 2008, when I start
to design this stadium,

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.960
and more people knows me
because I was architect.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.795
And then later when I
start to begin questioning

00:07:03.795 --> 00:07:08.624
the state's corruption and
all those kind of mishandling

00:07:08.624 --> 00:07:12.742
of schools building and which costs,

00:07:12.742 --> 00:07:17.742
over 5,000 students lost their life.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:21.800
And I've been totally
shattered off my internet

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.930
and also on the media.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:28.410
So, I guess, not so many people know me.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.470
I think that's fascinating

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:32.410
that you could be so famous
outside of your country,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.400
and yet inside your country,

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.359
you've been removed or
erased or disappeared,

00:07:37.359 --> 00:07:40.440
not physically, of course,
but just from the record.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.800
Because, how much do you
think people in China know

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.720
that they don't know things?

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.930
Well, China under the,

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.900
the world outside of China
is two different world,

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.980
is two parallel world.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:58.940
They hold very different
understanding about humanity,

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:03.920
about freedom of speech,
about political ideologies.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:08.186
So they openly ignore

00:08:08.186 --> 00:08:13.186
or criticize what is
happening in the West.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.490
So China have 1.4 billion people,

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:22.490
and they firmly believes
in communist propaganda.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:27.800
And that propaganda is very successful

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.940
and also they have very strong censorship.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:36.940
So they would make sure voice
like me will never be heard.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.070
And then I suppose that's,

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:41.080
you've got to question how successful

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.740
your activism is then if it's
for the rest of the world,

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.510
not for the Chinese.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.200
Well, they see the potential danger

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.200
of my activism online because
at that time for a moment,

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:58.680
I was quite quite vivid, you know.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.430
I raised a strong voice,

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.750
but that's why they have to put

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.730
this kind of punishment on me.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.070
But I wonder, you say in your book,

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.830
young people in China
today have no knowledge

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:16.770
at all of the student protests
in Tiananmen Square in 1989.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.390
And if they knew, they might not even care

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.002
for they learn submission
before they develop

00:09:22.002 --> 00:09:26.132
an ability to raise doubts
and challenge assumptions.

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:27.226
I think so.

00:09:27.226 --> 00:09:29.670
You know, they're kind of like a bird

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:34.670
has been caged for too long,
they cannot challenge to fly.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.640
What will China listen to?

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.713
Do you think a cultural boycott
would work, for instance?

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:43.653
I don't think so.

00:09:43.653 --> 00:09:45.298
I don't think anything,

00:09:45.298 --> 00:09:50.246
the West doing this kind
of boycott would work

00:09:50.246 --> 00:09:55.246
because simply China can suffer.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.780
You know, the government
is not gonna suffer,

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.320
but the people really understand

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:07.320
what is like when they
don't have that much.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:11.264
So in that kind of competition,
China can go very low,

00:10:11.264 --> 00:10:15.230
and I don't think the West
can compete with China.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:16.669
I was thinking about the cultural boycott

00:10:16.669 --> 00:10:19.900
because, of course, museums and galleries

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.200
still collaborate heavily in China.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.420
And yet, actually in the sports world,

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:26.570
we've seen anti-China messages

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:28.840
on certain sports people's shoes.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:31.090
Serena Williams has
come out, for instance,

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:32.300
recently for, Peng Shuai,

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.779
the Chinese tennis superstar
who made allegations online

00:10:34.779 --> 00:10:38.500
that she was sexually assaulted
by a Chinese official.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.740
Those allegations very quickly deleted.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.710
We should say she was also having

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:43.523
an affair with that individual.

00:10:43.523 --> 00:10:47.860
I just wonder, do you
think any of those actions

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:49.193
are with merit?

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:51.867
I think those actions

00:10:51.867 --> 00:10:56.640
are really helping the Western
public to understand China.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:01.550
But for Chinese, they know
this is not gonna work

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.840
because the big corporations in the West,

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:08.400
they're eager to make a
bigger profit in China.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.947
Nobody in the West in the corporate world

00:11:10.947 --> 00:11:13.680
will boycott China.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:18.680
So just a few sport men or
artists certainly will not work.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.570
I mentioned the tennis player, Peng Shuai,

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.380
talking about what happened to her.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:27.840
How brave do you have to
be to do what she did?

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:31.430
What she did is nothing to do with brave.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.263
Go on.

00:11:32.263 --> 00:11:36.250
You know, I think it's
also misinterpretation.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.280
She is a sport person,

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.390
which is like a soldier in the army.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.810
It's a race by Chinese state.

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:48.060
Any person in sport being considered

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.820
as the property of the party.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:54.830
So what she did, I don't
think it's a lot brave.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:58.020
She feel she has been mistreated

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:02.100
and then she posts on
her own personal blog,

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:06.664
or being deleted, then
later she performs according

00:12:06.664 --> 00:12:11.664
to the states will to let
her perform she's fine.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:17.760
And what is more disgusting
is the tennis association

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:25.290
under the Olympics jury
or Olympics committee,

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.448
trying to cover up.

00:12:27.448 --> 00:12:32.448
They're not really make her,

00:12:32.478 --> 00:12:35.990
demanding to have the truth out.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.540
I mean, you may not agree that it's brave.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:40.490
You see, you explain the reason
why you think she did it.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.420
I suppose it's just,

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.500
you talked about what can
happen to you in China,

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:48.490
and there is concern about
what will happen to her now.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.323
Oh, yes.

00:12:49.323 --> 00:12:52.723
She seeing horrible situation
because she made this,

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:58.920
you know, I don't know
if she is regret or not,

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.823
but she seems to now only perform

00:13:01.823 --> 00:13:04.990
on the same line as the state.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:07.217
And, of course, being forced.

00:13:07.217 --> 00:13:08.338
So it's business.

00:13:08.338 --> 00:13:09.333
That's the only hope.

00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:14.243
Business is dominating in
every corner of the world.

00:13:14.243 --> 00:13:17.740
Why do you think even cultural boycotts

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:20.720
haven't caught on in the west of China?

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.750
We see them of Israel, for instance,

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:25.580
but we don't see the
same levels of outrage

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:26.874
a lot of the time over the imprisonment

00:13:26.874 --> 00:13:28.710
of Uyghur Muslims, for instance,

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.080
who you mentioned earlier.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.174
Well, I don't know.

00:13:32.174 --> 00:13:36.628
Have you seen any
successful culture boycott

00:13:36.628 --> 00:13:41.317
which kind of shaking
a society like China?

00:13:41.317 --> 00:13:43.210
You know, it's not possible.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.683
And with many, many regions,

00:13:47.683 --> 00:13:51.003
culture boycott just simply doesn't work.

00:13:51.003 --> 00:13:53.046
China has been isolated,

00:13:53.046 --> 00:13:58.046
locked up for years
before, and they survived.

00:14:00.469 --> 00:14:03.333
Are you resigned to China
staying like this then,

00:14:03.333 --> 00:14:07.253
or you still, do you still
have fight in you, Weiwei?

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.850
I do fight all the time

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.333
because the fight is nature of my life.

00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:14.800
It's not because I want to win,

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:17.683
it's only because I have to fight,

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.100
I have no other choice.

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.730
Who are you fighting for now?

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:23.670
If we've established

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:27.190
that those in China don't
know you and can't see you,

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.600
and it's now you have to
live away from your mom

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.600
and you have to live in Portugal,

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:34.117
how effective can you be, do you think?

00:14:34.117 --> 00:14:35.760
I'm fighting for a lot of people

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:40.110
who's in same condition as me.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:43.500
We have been forced out from our land

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:46.464
in a way when we cannot
have a normal communication

00:14:46.464 --> 00:14:48.340
with our family.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.940
And because of all kinds of reasons.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:55.810
So we have to find a
way to express ourselves

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:58.780
and to let our voice to be heard.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:02.440
I was just, I was thinking
of the Russian Putin critic,

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:06.915
Alexei Navalny, who went
back in Russia, now in jail.

00:15:06.915 --> 00:15:09.933
Do you ever feel, have you
ever thought about going back

00:15:09.933 --> 00:15:12.783
because you can make that kind of impact?

00:15:14.349 --> 00:15:18.060
